{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwL3Fx1ZtFvnYr8YiGbZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check how the panels look. The rule's status is still \"pending\", so it hasn't run yet.\n\n**Data:** the logs data view uses `timestamp` as its time field. The fields I used were `response` (a string, so 5xx is matched as text), `extension`, `bytes`, `clientip`, `geo.*`, `machine.os`, `host`, `request` and `url`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-b27166f6 Web logs overview\" has four panels (http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-b27166f6-web-logs-overview-fc5768b292fb):\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Bytes by extension\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-b27166f6 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` where `response.keyword` matches `5*`. It fires when that count is above 10 within a 5-minute window.\n\nThe rule has no action attached, so it will show up as an alert in Kibana but won't send a notification anywhere. Also, the sample data's timestamps may not be recent, in which case the rule won't see many documents in its 5-minute window."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":19093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216},"output_tokens":436,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"81b01454-40ca-4f5c-ae2a-d73a5b75f12f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:37:13.559Z","request_id":"req_011CfwL3FiNknmxaJCz7j9Mg"}
